obo:FLOPO_0980586 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "cream sensu RHS Colour Chart fifth edition"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A colour quality for which RHS Colour Chart fifth-edition chip 158A or 158B is the specimen's closest visual match against a white background under artificial daylight conforming to CIE D6500."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Use only when the observation or protocol names RHS fifth-edition chip 158A or 158B. FLOPO-local source-qualified colour quality; its generic colour is PATO:0104031 (cream). Move this source-specific referent to a new FLOPO class; PATO:0104031 remains the generic cream parent."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-07-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.upov.int/documents/d/upov/tgp-documents-en-tgp_14.pdf> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0104031 .

obo:FLOPO_0980587 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "cream sensu Saccardo (1891)"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A colour quality recognized according to Saccardo's Chromotaxia as category 27, represented by cow-milk cream and described as white tinged faintly with yellow."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Use only when Saccardo's nomenclature or category 27 is specified. FLOPO-local source-qualified colour quality; its generic colour is PATO:0104031 (cream). The natural exemplar varies; the historical plate/category is the source-specific reference."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-07-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/chromotaxiaseuno00sacc> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0104031 .

obo:FLOPO_0980588 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "crimson sensu Wilson Horticultural Colour Chart (1938/1940)"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A colour quality recognized according to the Wilson Horticultural Colour Chart by closest match to chip H22, which the NIST source concordance places in ISCC-NBS block 11 vivid red."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Use only when the Wilson chart or H22 is specified. FLOPO-local source-qualified colour quality; its generic colour is PATO:0104314 (crimson). ISCC-NBS block 11 is a concordance classification, not a replacement for the physical H22 prototype."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-07-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:source <https://doi.org/10.6028/NBS.SP.440>,
        <https://doi.org/10.6028/jres.061.035> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0104314 .

obo:FLOPO_0980589 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "crimson sensu Textile Color Card Association of the USA"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A colour quality recognized according to the Textile Color Card Association of the USA by closest match to card 65013, which the NIST source concordance places in ISCC-NBS block 256 deep purplish red."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Use only when TCCA card 65013 is specified. FLOPO-local source-qualified colour quality; its generic colour is PATO:0104314 (crimson). This sense demonstrates why crimson cannot be assigned one unrestricted red prototype."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-07-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:source <https://doi.org/10.6028/NBS.SP.440>,
        <https://doi.org/10.6028/jres.061.035> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0104314 .

obo:FLOPO_0980590 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "scarlet sensu Saccardo (1891)"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A colour quality recognized according to Saccardo's Chromotaxia as category 15, represented by minium and pomegranate flowers and described as vivid red inclining slightly toward orange."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Use only when Saccardo's nomenclature or category 15 is specified. FLOPO-local source-qualified colour quality; its generic colour is PATO:0104317 (scarlet). The physical plate and stated exemplars define this historical sense."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-07-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/chromotaxiaseuno00sacc> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0104317 .

obo:FLOPO_0980591 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "scarlet sensu Ridgway (1912)"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A colour quality recognized according to Ridgway's 1912 standard by the specimen's closest match to the physical Scarlet chip on plate I at coordinate 5."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Use only when Ridgway 1912 or chip I 5 is specified. FLOPO-local source-qualified colour quality; its generic colour is PATO:0104317 (scarlet). Ridgway distinguishes Scarlet I 5 from Scarlet-Red I 3."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-07-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:source <https://doi.org/10.5962/bhl.title.144788> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0104317 .

obo:FLOPO_0980592 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "scarlet sensu Wilson Horticultural Colour Chart (1938/1940)"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A colour quality recognized according to the Wilson Horticultural Colour Chart by closest match to chip H19, which the NIST source concordance places in ISCC-NBS block 11 vivid red."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Use only when the Wilson chart or H19 is specified. FLOPO-local source-qualified colour quality; its generic colour is PATO:0104317 (scarlet). ISCC-NBS block 11 is a concordance classification, not a replacement for the physical H19 prototype."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-07-15"^^xsd:date ;
